1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,190
Your app sends out a million AI answers.

2
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:04,680
Before each one ships,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,880
a second model reads it and says <font color="#00FFFF">yes or no</font>.

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,580
At frontier prices, that one word

5
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:13,390
costs you <font color="#FF5252">$33,000</font>.

6
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:14,260
You are <font color="#00FFFF">the judge</font>.

7
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,180
An answer comes in with its source,

8
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:19,050
and you check whether it stays inside the source.

9
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:20,710
You run on a <font color="#FF5252">frontier model</font>,

10
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:23,200
so you pay frontier price for <font color="#FF5252">one word</font>.

11
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,610
There are two problems.

12
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:27,440
a) The <font color="#FF5252">bill grows</font> with every answer you check.

13
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:29,940
b) Your yes carries <font color="#FF5252">no weight</font>.

14
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:31,000
A sure yes

15
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:31,979
and a coin-toss yes

16
00:00:31,979 --> 00:00:34,001
look the same to the code that reads it.

17
00:00:34,001 --> 00:00:36,550
<font color="#FFD700">RULE ONE: move yes-or-no checks off the frontier model.</font>

18
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,060
Now you are <font color="#00FFFF">not allowed to write</font>.

19
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:42,250
You get <font color="#00FFFF">two boxes</font>, yes and no,

20
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,890
and you put a <font color="#00FFFF">number</font> on each.

21
00:00:43,890 --> 00:00:47,730
Yes <font color="#4ADE80">0.93</font>, no <font color="#FF5252">0.07</font>.

22
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:49,700
That is a <font color="#00FFFF">System One model</font>,

23
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:52,570
and <font color="#4ADE80">Jev</font> from TypeSafe is the first one.

24
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:54,640
You declare <font color="#00FFFF">the boxes</font> up front,

25
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:58,350
and every box comes back with a <font color="#00FFFF">probability</font> in one pass.

26
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,790
On 6,000 checks of financial research answers,

27
00:01:01,790 --> 00:01:07,080
<font color="#4ADE80">Jev</font> agreed with the frontier judge <font color="#4ADE80">91.5%</font> of the time.

28
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:11,140
At that rate, a million checks cost <font color="#4ADE80">$160</font>

29
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:13,120
instead of <font color="#FF5252">$33,000</font>.

30
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:16,490
A cheap open model costs $260,

31
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:19,760
so most of the saving is <font color="#00FFFF">leaving the frontier model</font>.

32
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,700
What <font color="#4ADE80">Jev</font> adds is <font color="#4ADE80">the number on each box</font>.

33
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:24,830
Draw a line at <font color="#FFD700">0.95</font>.

34
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:25,770
Above it <font color="#4ADE80">ships</font>,

35
00:01:25,770 --> 00:01:29,860
and between 0.6 and 0.95 goes to <font color="#00FFFF">a person</font>.

36
00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:32,890
<font color="#FFD700">RULE TWO: route on the probability, not on the word.</font>

37
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:34,810
It always picks one of your boxes.

38
00:01:34,810 --> 00:01:36,690
Testers sent a ticket classifier

39
00:01:36,690 --> 00:01:39,110
30 messages that fit no box.

40
00:01:39,110 --> 00:01:40,670
A <font color="#FF5252">cake recipe</font> came back

41
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:43,580
as a <font color="#FF5252">technical issue at 0.94</font>.

42
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,570
Not one of the 30 was <font color="#FF5252">flagged</font>.

43
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:47,480
It cannot return a wrong type.

44
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:50,280
It can return a <font color="#FF5252">wrong answer in the right type</font>,

45
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:52,830
with 0.94 on it.

46
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:55,440
<font color="#FFD700">RULE THREE: give every question a "none of these" box.</font>

47
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:58,217
How many labelled examples you need

48
00:01:58,217 --> 00:02:00,888
to place that line is the next part.

49
00:02:00,888 --> 00:02:03,850
<font color="#FFD700">Engineering track. Vault link in bio.</font>

